Question :-   What are various "𝗮𝘀 𝗮 𝗰𝗼𝗱𝗲" in Cloud ?

The “as a Code” concept is central to modern cloud computing and DevOps practices. It refers to representing and managing traditionally manual or configuration-heavy IT processes through code, which can be version-controlled, automated, and reproduced consistently.

Here’s a breakdown of the most common types of “as a Code” in cloud environments:-

𝟭. 𝗜𝗻𝗳𝗿𝗮𝘀𝘁𝗿𝘂𝗰𝘁𝘂𝗿𝗲 𝗮𝘀 𝗖𝗼𝗱𝗲 (𝗜𝗮𝗖)
Purpose: Automate infrastructure provisioning and management.
Tools: Terraform, AWS CloudFormation, Azure Resource Manager (ARM), Google Deployment Manager.

𝟮. 𝗖𝗼𝗻𝗳𝗶𝗴𝘂𝗿𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗮𝘀 𝗖𝗼𝗱𝗲 (𝗖𝗮𝗖)
Purpose: Manage and automate system configuration and application setup.
Tools: Ansible, Chef, Puppet
Example:
Installing and configuring NGINX, setting up users, or applying security baselines on servers.

𝟯. 𝗣𝗶𝗽𝗲𝗹𝗶𝗻𝗲 𝗮𝘀 𝗖𝗼𝗱𝗲 (𝗣𝗮𝗖)
Purpose: Define CI/CD pipelines declaratively in code.
Tools: Jenkinsfile (Jenkins), GitHub Actions, GitLab CI/CD, Azure Pipelines, CircleCI.
Example:
Writing a YAML file that automates build, test, and deployment steps.

𝟰. 𝗣𝗼𝗹𝗶𝗰𝘆 𝗮𝘀 𝗖𝗼𝗱𝗲 (𝗣𝗼𝗖)
Purpose: Enforce governance, compliance, and security rules programmatically.
Tools:  HashiCorp Sentinel, AWS Config Rules, Azure Policy.
Example:
Preventing deployment of untagged resources or enforcing encryption at rest.

𝟱. 𝗦𝗲𝗰𝘂𝗿𝗶𝘁𝘆 𝗮𝘀 𝗖𝗼𝗱𝗲 (𝗦𝗮𝗖)
Purpose: Integrate security practices into the development lifecycle via code.
Tools: Snyk, AWS Security Hub, HashiCorp Vault.
Example:
Scanning IaC templates for vulnerabilities before deployment.

𝟲. 𝗠𝗼𝗻𝗶𝘁𝗼𝗿𝗶𝗻𝗴 / 𝗢𝗯𝘀𝗲𝗿𝘃𝗮𝗯𝗶𝗹𝗶𝘁𝘆 𝗮𝘀 𝗖𝗼𝗱𝗲
Purpose: Define dashboards, alerts, and metrics collection in code.
Tools: Grafana dashboards, Prometheus rules, Datadog monitors as code.
Example:
Creating automated alert rules when CPU utilization exceeds thresholds.

𝟳. 𝗡𝗲𝘁𝘄𝗼𝗿𝗸 𝗮𝘀 𝗖𝗼𝗱𝗲
Purpose: Manage and automate network infrastructure programmatically.
Tools: Cisco NSO, AWS CDK, Terraform networking modules.
Example:
Creating subnets, load balancers, and security groups automatically.

𝟴. 𝗖𝗼𝗺𝗽𝗹𝗶𝗮𝗻𝗰𝗲 𝗮𝘀 𝗖𝗼𝗱𝗲
Purpose: Ensure regulatory and organizational compliance automatically.
Tools: Chef InSpec, AWS Config.
Example:
Automating HIPAA or PCI DSS compliance checks.

𝟵. 𝗕𝗮𝗰𝗸𝘂𝗽/𝗥𝗲𝗰𝗼𝘃𝗲𝗿𝘆 𝗮𝘀 𝗖𝗼𝗱𝗲
Purpose: Automate backup creation and recovery workflows.
Tools: AWS Backup as Code (CloudFormation/Terraform integration), Velero for K8s.
Example:
Defining policies to automatically back up EC2 or EBS volumes daily.
